Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||06-27-2000||02:34 AM||||are there full engine/tranny mount sets in polyurethane for fieros? would it hurt anything if i made my own dogbone bushings out of steel or metal? my bushings are very squishy (its an industry term) and if the car is braked and you let off the clutch while in gear, the engine moves quite a bit. almost 140k miles on it and the engine/tranny mounts are all original.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Taijiguy||06-27-2000||07:43 AM||||I wouldn't make the dogbone a solid mount using alminum or steel. The vibration would probably be unbareable for anything but racing. I installed a poly rebush kit from The Fiero Store (like 14 bucks) and it's a little raucous, but I like it. I've never seen poly engine and tranny monts, but that desn't automaticaly qualify me as an expert on the availability!<BR>Good luck<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||lowCG||06-27-2000||10:38 AM||||They cost $65 apiece from this place in California (Chris West),have thought about solid mounts,and using urethane on the cradle to allow for some give also.<BR>My dogbone has a couple of old shock mounting bushings stuffed into it,after grinding smooth the sharp obstruction inside,works great.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||06-27-2000||11:06 AM||||I've been really happy with NAPA replacement engine and transaxle mounts - not much engine movement, but the cockpit stays vibration-free.||||reg||1
